# llama.cpp's greedy continuation, for `hybrid_sweep`, `residency_sweep` and the forward-pass
# gate in `crates/moearc-engine/tests/gptoss_forward.rs`.
#
# model     gpt-oss-120b-MXFP4.gguf  (gpt-oss, 36 blocks, 128 experts, 4 active, MXFP4)
# prompt    "The capital city of France is"  ->  976 9029 5030 328 10128 382
#           tokenised with add_bos = false, which is what this file's
#           `tokenizer.ggml.add_bos_token` says.
# produced  llama-eval-callback with MOEARC_GREEDY_N=64, -ngl 0 (CPU backend)
# llama.cpp e107984bcffcfd701e82738092a2b000b6fda7a2
#
# 🔴 Verified identical on llama.cpp's own two backends — `-ngl 0` (CPU) and
# `-ngl 99 --n-cpu-moe 31` (SYCL) — before it was adopted. A greedy id is only a decision where
# the top two logits are further apart than the arithmetic difference between implementations,
# and on this model that difference reaches max|d| = 0.29 on the logit vector. The continuation
# below is a repeating nine-token cycle whose winner clears the runner-up by about 2.8.
#
# ⚠️ The sequence is 64 tokens and this model's sliding window is 128, so nothing here is
# affected by the SWA that `moe.rs` does not implement.

